Do not call glMapBuffer on OpenGL ES - it does not exist.

UploadDynamicBufferRegionImpl orphans a dynamic vertex buffer and then maps
it with glMapBufferARB. OpenGL ES has no glMapBuffer of any kind: ES 3.0
offers glMapBufferRange and GL_OES_mapbuffer offers glMapBufferOES, but the
ARB entry point is simply absent, so the loader leaves its pointer null and
the call jumps to address zero.

On the device that is a SIGSEGV with pc = 0 - the program counter itself,
not a null dereference - and the stack reads:

    pyrogenesis_main
      CRenderer::RenderFrame
        CSceneRenderer::PrepareScene            SceneRenderer.cpp:1152
          CMiniMapTexture::RenderFinalTexture   MiniMapTexture.cpp:534
            CMiniMapTexture::UpdateAndUploadEntities  MiniMapTexture.cpp:811
              UploadDynamicBufferRegionImpl
                pc 0x0

The minimap uploads its entity vertices through this path every frame, and
the minimap only exists once a match is running - which is why the menu was
fine and loading into a match closed the app.

On GLES the data is staged in a vector and handed over with one
glBufferSubData instead. The buffer is still orphaned first, so the driver
remains free to reallocate rather than wait for the previous contents, which
was the point of the mapping in the first place.

Both callers of UploadDynamicBufferRegionImpl go through this one function,
so this covers the memcpy variant as well.

The rest of the GL backend is careful about this: glDrawBuffer/glReadBuffer
in Framebuffer.cpp and the whole fixed-function path in ShaderProgram.cpp are
behind CONFIG2_GLES guards already. This one path was missed.

--- source/renderer/backend/gl/DeviceCommandContext.cpp
+++ source/renderer/backend/gl/DeviceCommandContext.cpp
@@ -137,6 +137,22 @@
 	glBufferDataARB(target, bufferSize, nullptr, GL_DYNAMIC_DRAW);
 	ogl_WarnIfError();
 
+#if CONFIG2_GLES
+	// OpenGL ES has no glMapBuffer at all. ES 3.0 offers glMapBufferRange and
+	// GL_OES_mapbuffer offers glMapBufferOES, but the ARB entry point used
+	// below simply does not exist, so the loader leaves its pointer null and
+	// calling it jumps to address zero - a SIGSEGV with pc = 0, from inside
+	// the minimap's entity upload, which is why this only ever happened after
+	// loading into a match.
+	//
+	// Stage the data and hand it over in one glBufferSubData. The buffer is
+	// still orphaned above, so the driver remains free to reallocate rather
+	// than wait for the previous contents.
+	std::vector<u8> staging(dataSize);
+	uploadFunction(staging.data());
+	glBufferSubDataARB(target, dataOffset, dataSize, staging.data());
+	ogl_WarnIfError();
+#else
 	while (true)
 	{
 		// (In theory, glMapBufferRange with GL_MAP_INVALIDATE_BUFFER_BIT could be used
@@ -160,6 +176,7 @@
 		// and hope it will eventually succeed
 		LOGMESSAGE("glUnmapBuffer failed, trying again...\n");
 	}
+#endif
 }
 
